  "interpretation": [
    "The original Control+A replacement failed: the second backend value appended to the first. That original failure and its exact tested source are retained. The next run uses native Home then Shift+End on this single-line input, followed by native insertText; its two backend iterations pass.",
    "Both original runs observe cookies and localStorage shared by simultaneous views and a reopened view despite dataStore=ephemeral. This is a fresh-view class, not fresh-context isolation.",
    "Disabled selector click resolves and emits trusted pointerdown but no click. Duplicate selectors select the first match; a covered target rejects on actionability timeout. These are observed semantic differences, not equivalent-action performance results.",
    "The declared exact-text MutationObserver helper is not a native matcher. Native missing-selector click timeout is a different operation and diagnostic contract. Native text replacement emits extra keyboard events compared with locator.fill.",
    "View closure rejects pending evaluation and later calls, but synchronous close does not attest target drain. Native closeAll kills the shared browser with SIGKILL. Both collectors adopt 4 terminal descendants and reject clean-observed-teardown, with no outer kill or survivors.",
    "Native launch policy differs from the shared comparator policy. The initial report called NUL-separated proc fields arguments; the final adapter labels them uninterpreted bytes because Chromium rewrites the process title. Neither report authenticates original argv.",
    "The final source matches the second run. The post-run competitor metadata update is separate; each run retains its originally captured configuration bytes. No source or numeric result is retroactively replaced."
  ],
